    "result_text": "All changes compile and the test suite is green. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Summary\n\nRedesigned the owner identity key to `identityKey = SHA-256 hex over (normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName))`, and reworked duplicate detection and soft-matching around it.\n\n### New file\n- **`mapper/IdentityKey.java`** \u2014 a shared helper providing:\n  - `of(telephone, email, lastName)` \u2192 full lower-case 64-hex SHA-256 over `telephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName)`.\n  - `soundex(lastName)` \u2192 standard American Soundex code (first letter + 3 digits, H/W treated as non-separating, vowels separating, zero-padded/truncated to 4).\n\n### Changes\n- **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 the `identityKey` DTO field now maps to `IdentityKey.of(telephone, email, lastName)` (was the plain `telephone|email|householdId` concatenation), so the returned key is a 64-char hex digest.\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**:\n  - `rejectDuplicate(...)` \u2014 409 detection now compares the new SHA-256 identity key (built from telephone + email + soundex of last name), still skipping `deleted` owners, still keeping the `sharesHousehold` bypass, and with the email-domain blocklist still applied first (in `normalizeEmail`, which runs before this). No longer takes/uses `householdId`, so the household-derived 409 path is gone; the single identity key is the only hard-duplicate rule. Two owners sharing last name + postcode but with different telephones now produce different keys \u2192 created, not rejected.\n  - `existingIdentityKey(...)` \u2014 derives the same SHA-256 key from a stored owner (E.164-normalizing the stored phone, lower-casing email, soundex of last name).\n  - `assignPossibleDuplicate(...)` \u2014 the soft match now fires when `soundex(lastName)` **and** `postcode` match but the `identityKey` **differs** (previously: exact last name + postcode + different telephone), lowest matching id wins; `sharesHousehold` still exempt.\n- Updated stale javadoc in `DuplicateOwnerIdentityException` and `ExceptionControllerAdvice` to describe the new key.\n\n### Tests\nFull suite (`AcceptanceTest`) passes: `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `coreIdentityKeyIsSha256Hex` (64-hex shape) and `coreRejectsDuplicateIdentity` (identical identity \u2192 409).\n\n`computeHouseholdId`/`householdId` are retained unchanged since they still drive `householdMemberCount` and the membership-level cap \u2014 they just no longer participate in the identity key.",
